BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Justice Film Night: 3 Shorts + Post-Screening Q&A
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260928T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260928T210000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1638334@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Movies
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerThree films. One powerful even
 ing exploring what becomes possible when communities organize to bring the
 ir people home from women’s prisons.\nPresented by the nonprofits UnComm
 on Law\, the California Coalition for Women Prisoners (CCWP)\, and the UC 
 Sentencing Project\, the evening will feature three short films:\n\nSol in
  the Garden\nFree Joan Little\nNo Time to Wait\n\nFollowing the screening\
 , we will host a Q&A with Sol Mercado\, Yoruba Richen\, and Chisa Hughes t
 o discuss incarceration\, race\, aging\, gender\, and freedom. Colby Lenz\
 , UnCommon Law’s Director of Policy and Advocacy\, will moderate the con
 versation.\n\n$5.00\n\nTickets: https://www.uncommonlaw.org/20th-community
 \nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/justice-film-night-3-shorts-postscreeni
 ng-qa-sf/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/CCWP-x
 -UCL-Film-Screening-Flyer-2026.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Delancey Street Screening Room\, 600 The Embarcadero\, San Franci
 sco\, CA 94107
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/justice-film-night-3-shorts-postscreening-qa-s
 f/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Filmscreening: Punking Punk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1639657@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Movies
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerPunk promised that anyone coul
 d get on a stage. It didn’t always keep the promise. These two documenta
 ries follow the people who held it to its word: the women who founded the 
 first all-female bands in Düsseldorf\, West Berlin\, and Zurich\, and the
  queer punks who built a scene of their own when the movement’s macho tu
 rn pushed them out. Two films\, one evening\, and the same refusal to ask 
 permission.\nEinfach machen! She-Punks von 1977 bis heute\nReto Caduff\, G
 ermany/Switzerland 2024\, 94 min\, German with English subtitles\n\n“Do 
 it! Don’t talk about it. Do it!” Martina Weith\, lead singer and saxop
 honist of Germany’s first all-female punk band Östro 430\, summed up th
 e movement’s radical practice in a single demand. Decades later\, the wo
 men who led pioneering bands like Mania D\, Malaria!\, and Kleenex are bac
 k on stage\, decrying patriarchy\, sexual repression\, dogmatic feminism\,
  and right-wing violence with the same electric fervor. Caduff’s nervy d
 ocumentary traces the story of the women of German-language punk — innov
 ators and provocateurs who fought as hard against bourgeois society as aga
 inst the subculture’s own machismo. With interviews from Weith\, Gudrun 
 Gut\, and Bettina Köster\, it looks back on punk’s contradictory gender
  dynamics and these women’s triumphant fight to plant their own black fl
 ag within it.\nQueercore: How to Punk a Revolution\nYony Leyser\, Germany/
 USA 2017\, 83 min\, in English\nWhile some of punk’s brashest arms-beare
 rs were enjoying...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.goethe.de/ins/us/en/st
 a/sfr/ver.cfm?event_id=27348315\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/filmscre
 ening-punking-punk/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Websit
 e-quer.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Goethe-Institut San Francisco\, 657 Howard Street San Francisco\,
  CA 94105
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/filmscreening-punking-punk/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mountains of the Moon — Live Film & Music Experience
