SUMMARY:Casino Royale (2006)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261005T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261005T204500
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17840705@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:CASINO ROYALE (2006) takes Bond back to his origins in an unus
 ual black-and-white foreword that hints at how the British agent earned hi
 s license to kill. The film is set in 2006\, and it's risky to ask audienc
 es to erase nearly 45 years worth of memories of a well-known character\, 
 but it's also fascinating to see the filmmakers wipe the slate clean and s
 tart again from the beginning.\n\nSecondly\, the film introduces Daniel Cr
 aig (the engaging anti-hero of the underrated crime drama LAYER CAKE) as a
  Bond who is still in the process of learning how to do his job\, much to 
 the consternation of his boss\, M\, played once again with exactly the rig
 ht amount of dry humor by Judi Dench.\n\nAs interpreted by Craig\, Bond is
  more energetic than he is suave and much more of a fighter than he is a l
 over. He makes some mistakes\, he gets temperamental\, he shows signs of v
 ulnerability\, and – best of all – he's not made of Teflon: when this 
 Bond gets into trouble\, he usually comes out with blood on his tuxedo and
  nasty-looking scratches on his face.\n\nTo the delight of Bond fans every
 where\, CASINO ROYALE reinvigorated the series and broke the bank at the b
 ox office.\n\nTickets: https://drafthouse.com/sf/show/casino-royale?cinema
 Id=0802&sessionId=21621\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/5/ca
 sino-royale-2006-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7562198;-122.419185
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34411150/116c3c27-26ca-4394-9608-db581b3c9257.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Alamo Drafthouse Cinema\, 2550 Mission St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/5/casino-royale-2006-tickets
END:VEVENT
