SUMMARY:Showgirls
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T124500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T144500
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17830873@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:One of the most derided movies of the 20th century is also one
  of its most spectacularly misunderstood. The odd-couple tag team of Dutch
  provocateur director Paul Verhoeven (ROBOCOP\, ELLE) and Sleazoid-Hungari
 an-American writer Joe Eszterhas (FLASHDANCE\, SLIVER) first came together
  with 1992's BASIC INSTINCT\, and everyone\, including the financial backe
 rs and the producer/distributors of this movie\, assumed lightning would s
 trike twice for the duo with 1995's SHOWGIRLS. Universally panned by criti
 cs upon its initial release\, people found the multi-tap combo of inane di
 alogue\, wild over-acting\, and extreme obscenity and grotesquerie to be j
 ust too much. Then the "so-bad-it's-good" crowd sunk their hollow claws in
 to the movie\, claiming it as one of the "best worst" movies of all time. 
 To be sure\, yes\, this is a movie in which Saved By the Bell's Elizabeth 
 Berkley sets fire to her TV-star image by grinding her pelvis on Kyle MacL
 achlan's lap until he simulates sexual climax while Gina Gershon watches. 
 She shoves chips into her mouth and reminisces about her days of eating an
 d enjoying "puppy chow\," between bouts of trying to make it as a Las Vega
 s showgirl "goddess."\n\nThe assumption that critics and chuckleheads alik
 e have made are that a) Verhoeven and Eszterhas weren't trying to make som
 ething with humor (they were)\, and b) that the surface story is meant to 
 be taken at face value (it's not). Verhoemie don't play that.\n\nSHOWGIRLS
  is a complicated\, satirical masterpiece that tes...\n\nTickets: https://
 drafthouse.com/sf/show/alamo-drafthouse-movie-book-club-showgirls?cinemaId
 =0802&sessionId=21338\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/11/sho
 wgirls-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7562198;-122.419185
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34368075/0ee791a5-14eb-45d3-83bf-cc401c827f94.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Alamo Drafthouse Cinema\, 2550 Mission St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/11/showgirls-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:9 to 5
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T160000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17796494@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Frameline & Another Planet Entertainment present\nA Tribute to
  Dolly Parton\n9 to 5\nFeaturing a drag performance by Peaches Christ\n\nS
 unday\, October 11 | The Castro\n\nWe can’t stay inside a lonely room an
 d cry forever\, so dry those tears and join Frameline (a few doors) down a
 t The Castro Theatre for a very special evening celebrating the life\, tal
 ents\, and values of the truly one-of-a-kind Dolly Parton. First\, Peaches
  Christ will pay tribute to the beloved “Jolene” singer with a drag ho
 mage\, and then we’ll start laughin' and drinkin' and havin' a party wit
 h a screening of 9 to 5.\n\nDirected by Colin Higgins (Harold and Maude)\,
  this cult classic centers on three women — the exuberant Doralee (Dolly
  Parton)\, the timid Judy (Jane Fonda)\, and the sharp-witted Violet (Lily
  Tomlin) — as they toil away at Consolidated Companies under the misogyn
 istic Mr. Hart (Dabney Coleman). When talking trash and sharing their wild
 est revenge fantasies isn’t enough\, the trio get even with their bigot 
 of a boss.\n\nWhether you love the film for its titular working-class anth
 em\, its satirical screwball comedy that skewers sexism in the workplace\,
  or the iconic trio at its center\, 9 to 5 is undeniably one of the late D
 olly Parton’s many great gifts to popular culture.\n\nA percentage of al
 l proceeds from ticket sales will be donated to Dolly Parton’s Imaginati
 on Library in honor of its founder.\n\nLuminary and Visionary Director Mem
 bers receive special access to this screening. Please log into your accoun
 t to...\n\n$25-$26\, All ages\nFrameline & Another Planet Entertainment pr
 esent: A Tribute to Dolly Parton\, Featuring Peaches Christ\nListed time i
 s doors\n\nTickets: https://www.frameline.org/films/frameline50/9-to-5\nDe
 tails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/11/9-to-5-featuring-a-drag-perf
 ormance-by-peaches-christ-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7619917;-122.4347365
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34206245/9025a38e-e221-484e-b6f6-1565ac13b46a.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:The Castro\, 429 Castro St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94114
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/11/9-to-5-featuring-a-drag-perform
 ance-by-peaches-christ-tickets
END:VEVENT
