DESCRIPTION:Post-screening Q&A with special guests to be announced.\n\nFil
 m Director and Writer Bobby Buccallato shares his documentary film debut o
 f Carter Country\, which follows the two-year journey of America’s most 
 unlikely Presidential candidate Jimmy Carter and his small town that follo
 wed him every step of the way.\n\nThis documentary seeks to capture the fo
 rgotten spirit of 1976\, the last great Presidential election of the 20th 
 century\, when a small town in Georgia suddenly became the political capit
 al of the world. This documentary is not the latest retelling of Jimmy Car
 ter. It is the first telling of the community (his community) and their co
 llective efforts that managed to lift up one of their own into The White H
 ouse.\n\nThis West Coast Premier is presented by the California Carter Ini
 tiative.\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 27m\n\nYear\n\n2026\n\nDirector\n\nBobby Buccell
 ato\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nCountry\n\nUSA\n\nLanguage\n\nEnglish\n\nFirst Sho
 wing\n\nOctober 18\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nFeatured\n\nTickets: https://ti
 cketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/22030?siteToken=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc4
 0c\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/18/carter-country-tickets
 \nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34488704/a6efbbcb-d028-4324-85ee-8b8574a952e3.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/18/carter-country-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Tale of Two Sisters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T131500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T151500
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17830865@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:If you think about it long enough\, anything can be supernatur
 al – your toothbrush\, a pair of sneakers\, or your parents. That’s wh
 at makes A TALE OF TWO SISTERS so terrifying. Sisters Soo-mi and Soo-yeon 
 arrive at their father’s country home to spend some quality time with th
 eir new stepmother. But there’s trouble in paradise. For proof\, check o
 ut the severed hands that live in a kitchen cabinet. The first Korean horr
 or movie to be distributed in America\, A TALE OF TWO SISTERS is a beautif
 ul hallucinogen. It’s quiet\, violent\, and visually stunning\, feeling 
 like a Korean version of THE SHINING as filtered through the adolescent pr
 e-angst of a Judy Blume novel if Judy Blume was secretly a demon. You’ll
  never see another haunted house movie like this one – and you’ll neve
 r forget it. (Joseph A. Ziemba)\n\nTickets: https://drafthouse.com/sf/show
 /sad-girl-cinema-club-a-tale-of-two-sisters?cinemaId=0802&sessionId=21343\
 nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/18/a-tale-of-two-sisters-tic
 kets\nSource: DoTheBay
